<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdallah Barshambu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1317</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdallah Barshambu was a king of Makuria in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, a member of the royal house who had become a Muslim while living at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. The Mamluk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nasir-muhammad">al-Nasir Muhammad</a> placed him on the throne in 1317, and an Arabic inscription records the conversion of the Throne Hall at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-dongola">Old Dongola</a> into a mosque in that year. He was soon overthrown and killed by Kanz al-Dawla of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kanz">Banu Kanz</a>.</p></div>
